flowchart TB
    accTitle: The contract with a real Paperless-ngx
    accDescr: Every Monday, when started by hand, and in a pull request that changes the app or the mock, the job paperless runs paperless-contract.sh for Paperless-ngx 2 and 3. It starts that Paperless with Redis, Nextcloud with the app and the mock, and assert_contract.py gives Paperless three synthetic text files. Then it checks, with the version of the API and the fields that the app asks for, the fields, dates, excerpts, pages and errors, the newest documents, the names of correspondents and types and what /api/ui_settings/ says an account may do directly, and the test of the connection, the warnings about the token and the results with their names through Nextcloud. The summary of the job shows the versions and every check. A broken contract fails the required check, so the pull request can't merge; a failed weekly run opens or updates the issue Paperless-ngx breaks the app, and a run that passes closes it.

    trigger["Weekly run, a start by hand,<br>or a pull request of the app<br>or the mock"]
    script["paperless-contract.sh<br>for Paperless-ngx 2 and 3"]
    start["Paperless-ngx and Redis,<br>Nextcloud with the app,<br>the mock"]
    seed["assert_contract.py gives Paperless<br>three synthetic text files"]
    direct["`Directly: fields, dates, excerpts,<br>pages, errors, the newest documents,<br>the names and what an account<br>may do, with *version=9*`"]
    through["Through Nextcloud: the test<br>of the connection, the warnings<br>about the token and the results<br>with their names"]
    holds{"The contract<br>holds?"}
    passed["The summary shows<br>the versions and every check;<br>the issue closes"]
    failed["The summary names the broken promise;<br>the pull request can't merge;<br>the weekly run opens or updates<br>Paperless-ngx breaks the app"]

    trigger --> script --> start --> seed --> direct --> through --> holds
    holds -- "yes" --> passed
    holds -- "no" --> failed

    classDef person fill:#f59e0b2e,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px
    classDef bot fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    classDef done fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    classDef fail fill:#dc26262e,stroke:#dc2626,stroke-width:2px
    class trigger person
    class script,start,seed,direct,through bot
    class passed done
    class failed fail
